>what is a vogan?
(Taking "vogan" to mean "vogon".)
Vogons are the Galaxy's most efficient bureaucrats and its least attractive
people. They demolished the Earth to build a hyperspace bypass, and have been
completing the paperwork ever since. Their poetry is also said to be dreadful.
Nobody has asked you to confirm this.

>please could you look

Arthur's Hut
A single round room of mud, thatch and optimism. Everything in it is exactly
where you left it, because there is nowhere else for it to be. A shelf runs
along one wall, and a bed, which is a bed on a generous day, takes up the other.
The doorway opens east onto the village green.

On the wooden shelf are a pencil sketch and a glass jar.

>i want to take the jar
Taken.

>/foo
There is no slash command called /foo. /HELP lists them.

>/

Commands outside the story start with a slash, as in a chat program:

  /SAVE  /RESTORE  /RESTART  /QUIT  /UNDO       the game itself
  /SCORE  /FULLSCORE  /NOTIFY ON|OFF            your progress
  /VERBOSE  /BRIEF  /SUPERBRIEF                 how much is described
  /SCRIPT  /UNSCRIPT                            a transcript of your game
  /HINT [BACK]  /DIFFICULTY  /ABOUT  /VERSION  /HELP    help
  /MACRO RECORD|STOP|PLAY|LIST|SHOW|DELETE   record and replay commands
  /INTRO  /HHGG                              overviews for newcomers

Everything else you type is part of the story. Plain English is fine, and so are
questions, such as WHO IS FORD PREFECT? Without the slash, those words are just
ordinary input, and the game will tell you if you needed one.

